# The Google Sheet, read only. Two layouts, and SHEET_ID wins when both are set.
#
# Preferred: the nine tab layout. Set SHEET_ID to the id in the address bar of
# the sheet. Pasting the whole address works too, the id is pulled out of it.
#
#   https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<SHEET_ID>/edit#gid=0
#
# Share the sheet as "anyone with the link can view". No publishing step is
# needed, because tabs are addressed by name rather than by gid.
#
# Tab names are exact and case sensitive:
#   Products, Claims, Worries          the content, required
#   Awareness, Spines, Slots, Goals,   the framework, all optional
#   Sections, Settings                 a missing one falls back to the built in value
#
# See the README for the columns each tab takes.
SHEET_ID=

# The original single tab layout, read only when SHEET_ID is unset. One flat
# table with a type column, content only, always the built in framework.
#
# In the sheet: File > Share > Publish to web > pick the single TAB (not
# "Entire document") > Comma separated values (.csv) > Publish. Copy the
# address it gives you. It looks like this, with a /d/e/2PACX- id that is not
# the same as the id in the address bar:
#
#   https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/2PACX-1vAbC.../pub?gid=0&single=true&output=csv
#
# The export form also works if the sheet is shared as "anyone with the link
# can view", and it does not need publishing:
#
#   https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<SHEET_ID>/export?format=csv&gid=<TAB_GID>
#
SHEET_CSV_URL=

# Where the tab requests go. Leave it unset in every real deployment. It exists
# so the nine tab path can be driven against a stand in sheet in a test.
# SHEET_BASE_URL=https://docs.google.com

# Server side only. Never exposed to the browser.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Postgres. Vercel Postgres, Supabase or Neon in production, local Postgres or a
# Neon dev branch for npm run dev.
#
# These four names are tried in order and the first usable one wins, because the
# Vercel and Supabase integrations write POSTGRES_URL rather than DATABASE_URL:
#
#   DATABASE_URL  POSTGRES_URL  POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL  POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING
#
# SUPABASE_URL is not one of them. It holds the REST endpoint rather than a
# connection string. The Supabase connection string is under
# Project settings > Database > Connection string, and the transaction pooler
# one on port 6543 is the right choice for serverless.
DATABASE_URL=
